== Match report ==

=== Sanrobonia 3–3 Asikyira (4–3 on penalties) ===
Co-hosts [[Sanrobonia national football team|Sanrobonia]] won the [[2026 AFA World Cup]] after a dramatic final against [[Asikyira national football team|Asikyira]] that was decided on penalties after a 3–3 draw.

The match was a thrilling contest from start to finish. [[Dante Palar]] opened the scoring for Sanrobonia in the 23rd minute, but [[Amadou Baal]] — the tournament's top scorer — equalised for Asikyira just three minutes later in the 26th. [[Gabriel Somba]] restored Sanrobonia's lead in the 41st minute, and the co-hosts went into half-time leading 2–1.

In the second half, Baal struck again in the 57th minute to bring Asikyira level at 2–2. Palar then scored his second of the match in the 69th minute to make it 3–2, and Sanrobonia looked set to lift the trophy. But in the first minute of stoppage time, [[Boubacar Sarr]] equalised for Asikyira to make it 3–3 and send the final to a penalty shootout.

