Sanrobonia won the shootout 4–3, with [[Ousmane Gueye]]'s miss in the fourth round proving decisive. [[Arman Daeng]] also missed for Sanrobonia, but [[Kofi Mensah]] was unable to capitalise.

== Summary ==

[[Sanrobonia national football team|Sanrobonia]] were crowned champions of the [[2026 AFA World Cup]], the first time the nation has won the tournament. The victory was especially sweet as Sanrobonia were co-hosts alongside [[Balisca]]. [[Dante Palar]] was the hero of the final, scoring twice in the match and converting the first penalty in the shootout.

[[Asikyira national football team|Asikyira]] finished as runners-up, with [[Amadou Baal]] finishing as the tournament's top scorer with 7 goals. The final was widely regarded as one of the greatest in AFA World Cup history, featuring six goals and a penalty shootout.

